{
 "what": "Engine-native movie subtitles for BFME2/RotWK 2.01 (AoR 10) campaign videos. Method taken from the Spanish submod traduccion-es 1.2.2 to do the same for Ukrainian. Works in game: checked by the user on 2026-11-18 with the Spanish mod (their files still carry the old note «SIN PROBAR EN EL JUEGO»). Our Overall_Game_Intro (CS01) currently has burned-in subtitles.",
 "files": {
  "data/ini/video.ini": "Each subtitled video needs «HasSubtitles = Yes» in its «Video <name>» block. AoR has 0 such lines; the Spanish mod adds 41 by shipping the WHOLE video.ini (whole-file override, must be re-merged after every AoR patch).",
  "data/<Language>/movies/<VideoName>.ini": "One file per video, named like the «Video <name>» entry (not like the .vp6 file). <Language> = game language from the registry (gi.dat GameRegPath). Our submod keeps the game in English, so the folder would be data/english/movies (the Spanish mod ships identical copies in data/english and data/spanish).",
  "lotr.str / lotr.csf": "Every Label used in the movie INIs must exist as SUBTITLE:<Label> in the string table; per the Spanish notes the game aborts at start-up if one is missing. For us: add the labels to our lotr.csf.",
  "data/ini/audiosettings.ini": "Spanish mod also sets AutomaticSubtitleLines 8 -> 4 (in-game voice subtitles, not movies), again by shipping the whole file.",
  "language.ini": "AudioSubtitleFont = \"Albertus MT\" 26 No = font of in-game voice subtitles (not movies)."
 },
 "movie_ini_format": "SubTitles <VideoName> / FontName = \"Arial\" / FontPitch = 16 / SubTitleType = CINEMA / SubTitle = Label:<Label> Color R:255 G:255 B:255 Style:SOLID Align:CENTER Line:<14|15> StartFrame:<n> EndFrame:<n> / End",
 "timing": "StartFrame / EndFrame = video frame index from 0 at THAT video's own frame rate: AoR videos are 24, 25, 23.976 or 30 fps (see AoR_10/movie_subtitles/fps.json; ffprobe r_frame_rate of the .vp6). frame = seconds * fps. The Spanish frames follow the real rates.",
 "label_naming": "Spanish labels: ES + video name without «_» + «_NN», e.g. ESAOTRCampaign00_01, ESAOTRCampaignROTK01a_03. Ours could be UA… the same way.",
 "line": "Line:14 / Line:15 = screen text row; the Spanish files alternate 14 and 15 (15 for two-row text).",
 "font": "Set per movie in its INI (FontName, FontPitch); colour per line (Color R G B). Must be a font the game knows: our submod ships albertusmt.otf (with Cyrillic) registered as «Albertus MT», so FontName = \"Albertus MT\" should work; «Arial» is the Windows system font (has Cyrillic, not the game look).",
 "english_source": "AoR's own campaign videos (AOTRCampaign*) have NO English subtitles in the game. lotr.str has only 240 old BFME2/RotWK SUBTITLE labels (CS11…, BAM…, BACO… for the old campaign intros). The Spanish team timed and wrote theirs from the audio. Their timings are reusable for any language; kept locally in 008_AoR/.temp/subtitles_es/es_reference.json (not in git: someone else's translation).",
 "status": "Method confirmed working in game (user ran the Spanish mod, 2026-11-18). Not implemented in our submod yet. Risks to keep in mind: whole-file overrides of video.ini / audiosettings.ini must be re-merged after AoR patches; a missing SUBTITLE label crashes the game at start-up.",
